---
title: Creating a Server Manager
description: Build control panel integrations for automatic hosting provisioning.
---

{% partial file="./_breaking-changes-caution.mdoc" /%}

Server managers connect FOSSBilling to hosting control panels (cPanel, Plesk, DirectAdmin, etc.), enabling automatic account creation, suspension, and management.

{% aside type="note" %}
These are for shared hosting control panels. For VPS or game servers, consider creating a product module instead.
{% /aside %}

## File Structure

Place your manager in:

{% filetree %}
- library/Server/Manager/
  - YourManager.php
{% /filetree %}

Extend `Server_Manager` and implement the required methods.

## Common Methods

FOSSBilling passes a `Server_Account` to account operations. See [`Server_Manager`](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Server/Manager.php) for every required method and its signature.

| Method | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `testConnection()` | Verify the server connection |
| `createAccount()` | Create a hosting account |
| `suspendAccount()` | Suspend an account |
| `unsuspendAccount()` | Restore a suspended account |
| `cancelAccount()` | Remove an account |
| `changeAccountPassword()` | Change the account password |
| `changeAccountPackage()` | Change the hosting package |

## Hestia Walkthrough

The bundled Hestia manager shows how FOSSBilling provisions and manages hosting accounts. [Hestia manager source](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Server/Manager/Hestia.php)

1. **Configure the server.** `getForm()` defines the access key ID and secret key fields. The manager’s `init()` checks that a hostname is configured. [Configuration code](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Server/Manager/Hestia.php#L16-L54)
2. **Test the connection.** `testConnection()` sends `v-list-users` to the panel and checks that it returns a success code. [Connection check](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Server/Manager/Hestia.php#L99-L115)
3. **Provision the account.** `createAccount()` uses the account, client, and hosting package details to create a panel user, then adds the domain. If the domain command returns an error code, the manager attempts to delete the new user before reporting the failure. [Provisioning code](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Server/Manager/Hestia.php#L137-L185)
4. **Manage the account.** `suspendAccount()`, `unsuspendAccount()`, and `cancelAccount()` use the account’s username to select the panel user. Each checks the panel’s return code before reporting success. [Account lifecycle methods](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Server/Manager/Hestia.php#L192-L261)

## Testing Your Manager

{% steps %}
1. [Add a test server](/admin-guide/server-managers/#add-a-hosting-server) and select your custom manager
2. Create a test hosting plan that your manager can provision
3. Create a **Hosting** product. Under **Hosting Settings**, select the test **Server** and **Hosting Plan**.
4. Place a test order and verify account creation in the control panel
5. Test suspend, unsuspend, and cancellation
{% /steps %}

